--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7ed8d592803d6492b8f1f0ac1555a1ea, type: 3}
  m_Name: Pairing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: InsightsSamples.Common::InsightsSamples.Common.SampleInfo
  id: 18-pairing
  number: 18
  title: Passcode pairing
  series: Without ArborXR MDM
  icon: key-round
  scenario: Front-desk device setup
  realWorld: "A front-desk device at a training center is being set up for the day. It isn't enrolled in ArborXR device management, so an admin pairs it once with a passcode from the Portal. From then on, every session on it reports to the organization's Insights."
  teaches: OnPairingStateChanged, StartPairing, ClearPairing, GetLastPairingRedeemResult
  sceneName: Pairing
  appWidePrefab: {fileID: 5954259378784827763, guid: 3b418866fa6f43ff8c7d52784ed01379, type: 3}
  whatThisShows: How a device without ArborXR MDM pairs with your organization, using
    a passcode from the Portal. A device ArborXR manages already has its organization,
    so none of this applies to it.
  tryThis:
  - In a WebGL or Android build, pair using a passcode from the Portal (Insights
    Hub, Pairing Passcodes).
  - 'Click Clear pairing: the pairing prompt comes back.'
  - 'Enter a wrong passcode: the prompt shows the Portal''s error and asks again, so
    you can enter the right one. Not now closes it, and the app carries on without
    Insights.'
  - 'Once paired, click Sign in again: the device signs in to your organization,
    as in sample 01.'
  - 'On a managed device, or a build that sends with an org token, Pair this device
    and Clear pairing are off. A WebGL build with no App Token of its own switches
    to pairing from the App button in the header: choose Pair with a passcode.'
  watchFor:
  - 'OnPairingStateChanged: Unpaired at startup, after Clear pairing, and after Not
    now; Paired after a passcode. A wrong passcode changes nothing, so it has no row.'
  - 'OnAuthCompleted: true once the device has paired.'
  lessonScript: PairingSample.cs
  lessonScriptLine: 39
  dashboardNotes: []
  expectedOnPass:
  - method: OnAuthCompleted
    name: signed_in
    count: 1
    atLeast: 0
    status: 
  expectedOnFail: []
